      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lutherbellhendricksv/{size}/2350_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-08-17T11:34:36.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"kitmehsu\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/kitmehsu/48/1901_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> kitmehsu:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Yet another thought on this line of reasoning, does proletariat get attack multiple times when more than one instance of him is in an area attack? Also, on the topic of who affects what, can a hero be affected by the track of one of their companion cards? I ask because of the hammer swing explicitly mentioning that other proletariat are immune.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Proletariat is unique in that he is one character, and yet many at the same time. If three Proletariats are hit by one area attack, they each defend separately. A companion's &nbsp;attack can damage the character and vice versa.</p>",
